<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdʒu.mu.ɑ">Jumu'ah</phoneme> briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">20032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Iran's strike cut a sixth of Qatar's liquefied natural gas exports, and Washington responded by rushing sixteen billion dollars in weapons to Gulf states — stopping well short of ground troops.</s> <s>Tehran has vowed zero restraint if struck again, while the White House seeks two hundred billion more from Congress to sustain a regional war without American soldiers on the ground.</s> <s>The Strait of Hormuz remains sealed, and every nation that depends on Gulf energy is now counting its reserves.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Venezuela's interim president, <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdɛl.si roʊˈdriː.ɡɛz">Delcy Rodriguez</phoneme>, replaced the entire military command within twenty-four hours — dismantling the security structure that kept Nicolás Maduro in power for over a decade.</s> <s>Rodriguez was installed after a United States-backed operation ousted Maduro in January, and President Trump has publicly claimed he effectively governs the country.</s> <s>Whether the new military leadership answers to Caracas or to Washington is now the defining question of Venezuela's transition.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Alexander <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="luˈkɑ.ʃɛŋ.koʊ">Lukashenko</phoneme> freed two hundred and fifty political prisoners on Thursday — the single largest release Belarus has made since the mass crackdowns of 2020.</s> <s>The move was not a change of conscience: it came from a deal, trading detainees for United States sanctions relief brokered by Trump envoy John <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="koʊl">Coale</phoneme>.</s> <s>More than eleven hundred people remain imprisoned, with no timeline for further releases as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="luˈkɑ.ʃɛŋ.koʊ">Lukashenko</phoneme> presses for full normalization.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Japan's Prime Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="sɑˈneɪ tɑˈkeɪ.tʃi">Sanae Takaichi</phoneme> told President Trump she intends to seek a direct summit with Kim Jong-un to secure the return of seventeen citizens Japan lists as North Korean abductees — a diplomatic push no Japanese leader has attempted since 2002.</s> <s>Hours later, Pyongyang displayed a new battle tank its state media described as resistant to missiles and drones, a show of force timed while United States military attention is fixed on the Hormuz crisis.</s> <s>No date or venue for any talks has been set.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Turkish police detained thirty-five people at a Wednesday rally in Istanbul's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="sɑˈrɑtʃ.hɑ.nɛ">Saraçhane</phoneme> square in support of Mayor <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɛkˈrɛm ɪˌmɑːˈmoʊ.lu">Ekrem İmamoğlu</phoneme>, who has been jailed for a year.</s> <s>Four of those detained now face unannounced charges — a direct test of Turkey's constitutional right to peaceful assembly.</s> <s>The square has become a weekly arrest site.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Namibia, opposition lawmakers called the government's new budget treasonous, accusing the ruling <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈswɑː.poʊ">Swapo</phoneme> party of breaking its promise to protect the poor from inflation in one of the world's most unequal societies.</s> <s>The budget raises the monthly pension by one hundred Namibian dollars — roughly five United States dollars — while energy and food costs continue to climb.</s> <s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈswɑː.poʊ">Swapo</phoneme>'s parliamentary majority is expected to carry the vote regardless.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Gold has fallen five hundred and eleven dollars an ounce since the Iran war began — the opposite of what markets do in a typical crisis.</s> <s>Investors normally drawn to gold as a safe haven are instead selling it to cover energy margin calls as oil prices spike with the Hormuz closure, and traders in Dubai are offloading the metal forty dollars below market just to exit positions.</s> <s>Analysts expect prices to fall further if the conflict expands.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea declared a crude oil supply emergency on Friday, with the sealed Strait of Hormuz cutting off seventy percent of its crude imports and leaving the country an estimated two hundred and eight days of reserves at reduced consumption.</s> <s>The vice industry minister warned refiners may be ordered to divert oil from export to domestic supply.</s> <s>Samsung Heavy meanwhile won a two hundred and fifty-three million dollar contract for a new liquefied natural gas carrier — a signal that Pacific energy corridors are already being rebuilt for a world without Hormuz access.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Astronomers studying the third interstellar object ever confirmed — a comet designated Three-I ATLAS — found its deuterium levels running thirty times higher than Earth's oceans, the most extreme ratio ever measured in any known body.</s> <s>That concentration means the comet formed near absolute zero in another star system, carrying a chemical fingerprint nothing in our solar system could produce.</s> <s>Researchers have only weeks to observe it before it passes beyond reach forever.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China joined an international nuclear energy pledge on Thursday, framing atomic power alongside renewables as its official decarbonization model — significant because China is currently building more reactors than any other nation on Earth.</s> <s>Beijing also enacted its first comprehensive environmental law this week, the Ecological Code, with binding targets for local governments.</s> <s>Whether China's coal-mine methane emissions — which shifted to deeper, more potent seams after a 2015 industry consolidation — will be fully accounted for at COP Thirty in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="bɛˈlɛm">Belém</phoneme> later this year remains a contested question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers Charles Bennett and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʒiːl brɑˈsɑːr">Gilles Brassard</phoneme> won the 2025 Turing Award for a quantum encryption protocol they invented poolside in 1979 — one that makes any eavesdropper mathematically detectable, regardless of their computing power.</s> <s>Their BB Eighty-Four protocol now underpins quantum-secure networks in China and Europe, and its urgency grows as quantum computers edge closer to breaking conventional encryption.</s> <s>The award is a reminder that the most consequential ideas can arrive decades before the world is ready for them.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Category Four Cyclone <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="nəˈrɛl">Narelle</phoneme> struck the northern tip of Queensland, Australia, on Friday, bringing what forecasters called the strongest winds the region has seen in decades.</s> <s>Remote coastal towns and Indigenous communities with limited evacuation routes bore the brunt, and Queensland's premier warned conditions would worsen before easing.</s> <s>Australia's Bureau of Meteorology is tracking the system as it pushes inland.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's new Social Media Protection and Regulatory Authority took effect this week, granting the government power to block any platform outright if it refuses to register or comply with its orders.</s> <s>The authority was created under a cybercrime law that Amnesty International calls repressive, and its first chairman is Islamabad's own Advocate General — a government lawyer now empowered to regulate the companies he may suspend.</s> <s>Platforms serving Pakistan's two hundred and forty million people face a choice between compliance and shutdown.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>